From: rocjitsu vfio-user development
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: skip compute IB tests when MEC firmware not loaded

When running in vfio-user emulation with fw_load_type=0, the MEC
firmware is not loaded (mec_fw_version stays 0) and the CP command
processor never executes. In this case, the compute ring DRM
schedulers are initialized but the compute queues are never mapped
(KCQ enable via KIQ submits PM4 packets that never run).

If amdgpu_ib_ring_tests() then tries to submit IB jobs on these
compute rings, drm_sched_job_init() dereferences a null sched->ops
pointer and the kernel panics with "modprobe exited with irqs disabled".

Fix by skipping IB tests on COMPUTE rings when mec_fw_version == 0,
which reliably indicates the CP firmware has not been loaded and the
compute scheduler is not functional.

Applies to: ROCm amdgpu roc-7.2.x
Tested on:  kernel 7.0.0-28-generic, Ubuntu 24.04 Noble

--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ib.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_ib.c
@@ -449,6 +449,14 @@ int amdgpu_ib_ring_tests(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 		if (!ring->sched.ready || !ring->funcs->test_ib)
 			continue;
 
+		/* Skip IB tests on compute rings when MEC firmware has not
+		 * loaded (fw_load_type=0 leaves mec_fw_version as 0). In
+		 * vfio-user emulation the CP never executes so compute ring
+		 * schedulers are initialized but queue mapping never runs,
+		 * causing drm_sched_job_init to dereference null ops. */
+		if (ring->funcs->type == AMDGPU_RING_TYPE_COMPUTE &&
+		    adev->gfx.mec_fw_version == 0)
+			continue;
+
 		if (adev->enable_mes &&
 		    ring->funcs->type == AMDGPU_RING_TYPE_KIQ)
 			continue;
